        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(channels): progress drafts only for long tasks, with the model's own preamble as the status headline",
        "body": "Closes #105872\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes progress drafts appearing for small tasks even though the draft gate nominally waits five seconds. The second work event bypassed that delay, and the utility narrator could spend a model call before any draft was visible. Progress-mode channels also discarded the model's typed preamble even though it is the most accurate status headline available.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe draft gate is now purely time-based; explicit immediate paths such as approvals and patches remain immediate. Utility narration starts only after the draft becomes visible. The shared compositor prefers fresh, typed model preambles as the headline, then uses utility narration only when the preamble is absent or stale. No config or model-facing tool surface was added.\n\nThe implementation preserves preamble item identity and retractions, counts only sanitized commentary that the compositor accepts, cancels narrator retries and expiry timers when a turn settles, rejects stale in-flight utility results, resets queued-turn lifecycle state, and refreshes same-text headlines when a new preamble item arrives.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Fast turns produce only the final answer: no transient draft, receipt, or utility narration call.\n- Long turns show the model's current preamble as the status headline, with utility narration filling genuine silences and tool activity retained below it.\n- Retractions clear the matching headline, final delivery removes the draft, and queued turns begin with fresh lifecycle state.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Frozen reviewed head: `0d5272b6e0b4e45ca29e8f5eeeb5e2e6d2288c0e`, rebased onto `c3505182ba26a1fb772d7b5d9342ab84c612e0ef`.\n- Blacksmith Testbox lease `tbx_01kxep81fezdaz4txwzj88y3wd`; hydration/run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29286632660.\n- All ten touched test files passed: 1,081 tests across plugin SDK, auto-reply, Discord, Telegram, Matrix, Teams, Slack, and the shared compositor.\n- Hosted CI found one stale generated docs-map heading after the docs rename; `docs/docs_map.md` is regenerated and `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check` passes on the final head.\n- Exact-final-head CI has one unrelated current-main failure: `extensions/lobster` dependency detection. Clean main `908230a53783` reproduces the same 1 failure / 430 passes in `src/plugins/contracts/extension-runtime-dependencies.contract.test.ts` on Testbox run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29287663357. This PR does not touch Lobster or that contract.\n- Shared OpenClawKit Periphery also reports three unrelated Swift identities in https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29287392859; this PR changes no `apps/**` files.\n- Fresh autoreview found and drove one final same-text/new-item freshness repair; the follow-up review returned no accepted or actionable findings.\n- Hosted CI exposed a plugin boundary contract gap. The follow-up exports the channel-owned progress lifecycle options through `GetReplyOptions`; exact-head `pnpm tsgo:prod`, all 121 extension package boundary compiles, the plugin SDK API baseline, and a fresh autoreview are green.\n- Direct Codex protocol contract checked: `../codex/codex-rs/protocol/src/models.rs` defines commentary/final message phases; `../codex/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v2/item.rs` carries agent-message `id`, `text`, and `phase`; `../codex/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/event_mapping.rs` maps content deltas to agent-message deltas.\n- Telegram Desktop proof requested at https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/106026#issuecomment-4962589069. The first workflow attempt timed out during duplicate baseline/candidate builds before capture; the stale-head rerun was canceled after the docs-map fix. Exact-final-head rerun: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29287399150. Discord uses the same compositor and settlement lifecycle, with 131 focused Discord tests in the exact-head run.\n",
        "branch": "claude/activity-summaries-complex-tasks-af13f0",
